OL,3,GNEWSARoger's colleagues step up after
OL,4,Ainjury ends BBC presenter's running
OL,5,Achallenge
OL,6,
OL,7,FI'm not much of a runner. I never have
OL,8,Fbeen.
OL,10,FBut I have been getting my trainers on
OL,11,Fmost mornings for the past 18 months,
OL,12,Fsimply to stay fit and lose weight.
OL,14,FSo, I wasn't too daunted when I was
OL,15,Fchallenged to run 26.2 miles (41km)
OL,16,Fover the space of two weeks for this
OL,17,Fyear's BBC Children in Need appeal.
OL,19,FLots of people do a marathon in one go,
OL,20,Fso how hard could it be?
